   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyoVQ",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "I know Kiwis care about each other and our place. New Zealand Aotearoa can be a place where everyone thrives together. There's enough for everyone to live affordable lives through taxing extreme wealth, lowering power, food, transport and other bills. We all benefit from healthy nature, where we can drink, swim, and fish in our oceans and rivers. We need honest government able to deliver, and this is my purpose as a Green MP."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyoXb",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I was born in Ōtepoti Dunedin and grew up in rural Otago. From studying and teaching at the University of Otago, to running an NGO working on energy and climate solutions and working for a kaupapa Māori organisation to eliminate energy poverty, I've invested in solutions for some of our most wicked problems. As an MP I've prepared the path for cheaper, cleaner, smarter power for all of us, and I'm ready to deliver."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyoZm",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Advocate for central government investment in South Dunedin and community-led adaptation efforts."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyobx",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Reduce cost-of-living pressures through affordable power, food and cheaper transport options."
     },
     {
      "_key": "RIU5sv1nWnkj6dpEqoyoe8",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Enable local energy solutions for households, farms, businesses, & iwi to build energy resilience."
     }
    ],
